Specifically:

  Sources/MusterMac/KeyTranslation.swift ports the NSEvent-to-key-event heuristics
  from macos/Sources/Ghostty/NSEvent+Extension.swift - which modifiers a keyboard
  layout consumed, how to read an unshifted codepoint, and which characters must
  not reach a terminal as text.

  Sources/MusterMac/FindBar.swift ports the find bar from
  macos/Sources/Ghostty/Surface View/SurfaceView.swift (SurfaceSearchOverlay) and
  macos/Sources/Helpers/Backport.swift (BackportSelectionTextField) - the layout,
  the corner-snapping drag, the button style, and what escape and return do. What
  it counts is Muster's own: the search runs in Muster's core against history held
  by a session daemon, not in the renderer.

  Sources/MusterCore/Input/Key.generated.swift and
  Sources/MusterVT/KeyMapping.generated.swift are generated from Ghostty's
  src/input/keycodes.zig, itself derived from Chromium's DOM code table
  (BSD-style license).

Muster also links libghostty and libghostty-vt from the same project. Those are
built from source at the commit pinned in deps/ghostty.pin and are not vendored
here.

Muster's app bundle redistributes herdr (https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr),
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The binary is the release named
in deps/herdr.pin, unmodified; a copy of its license ships beside it in the
bundle and is kept at licenses/herdr/LICENSE. Muster starts that daemon and
speaks to it over its socket, and contains no herdr source.

